---@field priorRevisionTags? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringList Optional. A list of tags that are added to the prior revision while the canary phase is in progress.
---@field canaryRevisionTags? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringList Optional. A list of tags that are added to the canary revision while the canary phase is in progress.
---@field stableRevisionTags? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringList Optional. A list of tags that are added to the final stable revision when the stable phase is applied.
---@field automaticTrafficControl? boolean Optional. Whether Cloud Deploy should update the traffic stanza in a Cloud Run Service on the user's behalf to facilitate traffic splitting. This is required to be true for CanaryDeployments, but optional for CustomCanaryDeployments.

---Information specifying where to deploy a Cloud Run Service.
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.CloudRunLocation
---@field location? string Required. The location for the Cloud Run Service. Format must be `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`.

---CloudRunMetadata contains information from a Cloud Run deployment.
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.CloudRunMetadata
---@field revision? string Output only. The Cloud Run Revision id associated with a `Rollout`.
---@field previousRevision? string Output only. The previous Cloud Run Revision name associated with a `Rollout`. Only set when a canary deployment strategy is configured. Format for service is projects/{project}/locations/{location}/services/{service}/revisions/{revision}. Format for worker pool is projects/{project}/locations/{location}/workerPools/{workerpool}/revisions/{revision}.
---@field job? string Output only. The name of the Cloud Run job that is associated with a `Rollout`. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/jobs/{job_name}`.
---@field serviceUrls? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringList Output only. The Cloud Run Service urls that are associated with a `Rollout`.
---@field service? string Output only. The name of the Cloud Run Service that is associated with a `Rollout`. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/services/{service}`.
---@field workerPool? string Output only. The Cloud Run worker pool associated with a `Rollout`. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/workerPools/{worker_pool}`.

---CloudRunRenderMetadata contains Cloud Run information associated with a `Release` render.
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.CloudRunRenderMetadata
---@field job? string Output only. The name of the Cloud Run Job in the rendered manifest. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/jobs/{job}`.
---@field service? string Output only. The name of the Cloud Run Service in the rendered manifest. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/services/{service}`.
---@field workerPool? string Output only. The name of the Cloud Run Worker Pool in the rendered manifest. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/workerPools/{worker_pool}`.
---@field revision? string Output only. The name of the Cloud Run Revision in the rendered manifest. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/services/{service}/revisions/{revision}`.

---Represents a whole or partial calendar date, such as a birthday. The time of day and time zone are either specified elsewhere or are insignificant. The date is relative to the Gregorian Calendar. This can represent one of the following: * A full date, with non-zero year, month, and day values. * A month and day, with a zero year (for example, an anniversary). * A year on its own, with a zero month and a zero day. * A year and month, with a zero day (for example, a credit card expiration date). Related types: * google.type.TimeOfDay * google.type.DateTime * google.protobuf.Timestamp
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.Clouddeploy_Date
---@field month? number Month of a year. Must be from 1 to 12, or 0 to specify a year without a month and day.
---@field day? number Day of a month. Must be from 1 to 31 and valid for the year and month, or 0 to specify a year by itself or a year and month where the day isn't significant.
---@field year? number Year of the date. Must be from 1 to 9999, or 0 to specify a date without a year.

---Retries the failed job.
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.Clouddeploy_Retry
---@field backoffMode? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.Clouddeploy_RetryBackoffModeEnum|string Optional. The pattern of how wait time will be increased. Default is linear. Backoff mode will be ignored if `wait` is 0.
---@field attempts? string Required. Total number of retries. Retry is skipped if set to 0; The minimum value is 1, and the maximum value is 10.
---@field wait? string Optional. How long to wait for the first retry. Default is 0, and the maximum value is 14d.

---@alias gcp.clouddeploy_v1.Clouddeploy_RetryBackoffModeEnum "BACKOFF_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BACKOFF_MODE_LINEAR"|"BACKOFF_MODE_EXPONENTIAL"

---Service-wide configuration.
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.Config
---@field name? string Name of the configuration.
---@field supportedVersions? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.SkaffoldVersionList All supported versions of Skaffold.
---@field defaultToolVersions? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.ToolVersions Output only. Default tool versions. These tool versions are assigned when a Release is created without specifying tool versions.
---@field defaultSkaffoldVersion? string Default Skaffold version that is assigned when a Release is created without specifying a Skaffold version.

---This task is represented by a container that is executed in the Cloud Build execution environment.
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.ContainerTask
---@field env? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringMap Optional. Environment variables that are set in the container.
---@field args? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringList Optional. Args is the container arguments to use. This overrides the default arguments defined in the container image.
---@field image? string Required. Image is the container image to use.
---@field command? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringList Optional. Command is the container entrypoint to use. This overrides the default entrypoint defined in the container image.

