---A `Target` resource in the Cloud Deploy API. A `Target` defines a location to which a Skaffold configuration can be deployed.
---@class gcp.clouddeploy_v1.Target
---@field gke? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.GkeCluster Optional. Information specifying a GKE Cluster.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the `Target`. Max length is 255 characters.
---@field etag? string Optional. This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of other fields, and may be sent on update and delete requests to ensure the client has an up-to-date value before proceeding.
---@field labels? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringMap Optional. Labels are attributes that can be set and used by both the user and by Cloud Deploy. Labels must meet the following constraints: * Keys and values can contain only lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores, and dashes. * All characters must use UTF-8 encoding, and international characters are allowed. * Keys must start with a lowercase letter or international character. * Each resource is limited to a maximum of 64 labels. Both keys and values are additionally constrained to be <= 128 bytes.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Most recent time at which the `Target` was updated.
---@field uid? string Output only. Unique identifier of the `Target`.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time at which the `Target` was created.
---@field annotations? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringMap Optional. User annotations. These attributes can only be set and used by the user, and not by Cloud Deploy. See https://google.aip.dev/128#annotations for more details such as format and size limitations.
---@field deployParameters? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.StringMap Optional. The deploy parameters to use for this target.
---@field run? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.CloudRunLocation Optional. Information specifying a Cloud Run deployment target.
---@field multiTarget? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.MultiTarget Optional. Information specifying a multiTarget.
---@field executionConfigs? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.ExecutionConfigList Optional. Configurations for all execution that relates to this `Target`. Each `ExecutionEnvironmentUsage` value may only be used in a single configuration; using the same value multiple times is an error. When one or more configurations are specified, they must include the `RENDER` and `DEPLOY` `ExecutionEnvironmentUsage` values. When no configurations are specified, execution will use the default specified in `DefaultPool`.
---@field associatedEntities? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.AssociatedEntitiesMap Optional. Map of entity IDs to their associated entities. Associated entities allows specifying places other than the deployment target for specific features. For example, the Gateway API canary can be configured to deploy the HTTPRoute to a different cluster(s) than the deployment cluster using associated entities. An entity ID must consist of lower-case letters, numbers, and hyphens, start with a letter and end with a letter or a number, and have a max length of 63 characters. In other words, it must match the following regex: `^[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$`.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the `Target`. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/targets/{target}`. The `target` component must match `[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?`
---@field customTarget? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.CustomTarget Optional. Information specifying a Custom Target.
---@field targetId? string Output only. Resource id of the `Target`.
---@field requireApproval? boolean Optional. Whether or not the `Target` requires approval.
---@field anthosCluster? gcp.clouddeploy_v1.AnthosCluster Optional. Information specifying an Anthos Cluster.

